# Negative Student Attitudes and the Teaching of the Humanities.

**Authors:** Keaveney, Madeline W.

## Abstract
In light of declining enrollments and decreasing funding in colleges and universities, humanities curricula should be reorganized to overcome negative student attitudes toward humanities courses. Recounts the successful use of collaborative learning experiences in teaching poetry and suggests the development of interdisciplinary career-option minors. (DMM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ260156

